\title{Basis for a Topology}
\taxon{Definition}
\p{
    Let #{(X,\tau)} be a [topological space](def-000C). A collection
    #{\mathcal{B}\subseteq\tau} is a \strong{basis} for #{\tau} if, whenever
    #{U\in\tau} and #{x\in U}, there is some #{B\in\mathcal{B}} such that
    ##{
        x\in B\subseteq U.
    }
    Equivalently, every open set is a union of members of #{\mathcal{B}}.
}
\p{
    A collection #{\mathcal{B}\subseteq\mathcal{P}(X)} generates a topology
    by taking arbitrary unions of its members provided that it covers #{X} and
    satisfies the refinement condition
    ##{
        x\in B_1\cap B_2
        \quad\Longrightarrow\quad
        \exists B_3\in\mathcal{B},\;
        x\in B_3\subseteq B_1\cap B_2.
    }
}
